a:2:{s:7:"current";a:7:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1744273761;s:8:"modified";i:1729665586;}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:11:"description";a:1:{s:8:"abstract";s:503:"# Assessment of CIRP Timelines

This study, commissioned by the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India (IBBI), analyzes delays in the Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process (CIRP) in India. The research focuses on identifying specific stages within the CIRP where delays are most common and explores whether certain sectors experience more delays than others. The study uses both primary and secondary data: analysis of CIRP forms and a survey of insolvency professionals. The findings reveal that…";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:11:"last_change";a:10:{s:4:"date";i:1729665586;s:2:"ip";s:9:"127.0.0.1";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:59:"articles:opinion_articles:03.09_assessment_of_cirp_timeline";s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:3:"sum";s:23:"created - external edit";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:26565;s:9:"timestamp";i:1729665586;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1744273761;}s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:7:"creator";s:0:"";s:11:"last_change";a:10:{s:4:"date";i:1729665586;s:2:"ip";s:9:"127.0.0.1";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:59:"articles:opinion_articles:03.09_assessment_of_cirp_timeline";s:4:"user";s:0:"";s:3:"sum";s:23:"created - external edit";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:26565;s:9:"timestamp";i:1729665586;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}}}